Test ID     hardBinding
Comment     iterate this
Client ID   1
Engine      MuPAD
Command ID	Fixup
 <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
   <mo>[</mo>
   <mi>s</mi>
   <mi>sin</mi>
   <mi>s</mi>
   <mi>cos</mi>
   <mi>t</mi>
   <mo>,</mo>
   <mi>s</mi>
   <mi>cos</mi>
   <mi>s</mi>
   <mi>cos</mi>
   <mi>t</mi>
   <mo>,</mo>
   <mi>s</mi>
   <mi>sin</mi>
   <mi>t</mi>
   <mo>]</mo>
 </math>
End of test


SetClientPref     1,use_mfenced,0

Passthru    <hr/><h3>New with &lt;mrow></h3>
Test ID     absolute value as fence
Comment     base
Client ID   1
Engine      MuPAD
Command ID	Fixup
  <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
    <mfenced ilk="enclosed-list" open="[" close="]">
      <mfrac>
        <mn>1</mn>
        <msqrt>
          <mfenced open="(" close=")">
            <mrow>
              <mn>1</mn>
              <mo>+</mo>
              <msup>
                <mfenced open="|" close="|">
                  <mrow>
                    <msup>
                      <mi>y</mi>
                      <mn>2</mn>
                    </msup>
                    <mo>-</mo>
                    <msup>
                      <mi>t</mi>
                      <mn>2</mn>
                    </msup>
                  </mrow>
                </mfenced>
                <mn>2</mn>
              </msup>
            </mrow>
          </mfenced>
        </msqrt>
      </mfrac>
      <mfrac>
        <mrow>
          <msup>
            <mi>y</mi>
            <mn>2</mn>
          </msup>
          <mo>-</mo>
          <msup>
            <mi>t</mi>
            <mn>2</mn>
          </msup>
        </mrow>
        <msqrt>
          <mfenced open="(" close=")">
            <mrow>
              <mn>1</mn>
              <mo>+</mo>
              <msup>
                <mfenced open="|" close="|">
                  <mrow>
                    <msup>
                      <mi>y</mi>
                      <mn>2</mn>
                    </msup>
                    <mo>-</mo>
                    <msup>
                      <mi>t</mi>
